      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "15149e42-c395-54e8-80bb-054b5cc8ccbf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred Döblin, César Vallejo\n- Works: Berlin Alexanderplatz, Tales of a Long Night, Los heraldos negros\n- Roles: novelist, essayist, doctor, poet, writer, playwright, journalist\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred Döblin was born on 10 August 1878 and died on 26 June 1957.\n- César Vallejo was born on 16 March 1892 and died on 15 April 1938.\n- César Vallejo was a Peruvian poet, writer, playwright, and journalist.\n- Alfred Döblin was a German novelist, essayist, and doctor.\n- César Vallejo wrote the poems in Los heraldos negros between 1915 and 1918.\n- Los heraldos negros was published in July 1919 as a collection of poems by César Vallejo.\n- Berlin Alexanderplatz was published in 1929 and is the novel for which Alfred Döblin is best known.\n- Tales of a Long Night, also titled Hamlet oder Die lange Nacht nimmt ein Ende, was published in 1956 as Alfred Döblin’s last novel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
